	(text "The video card V3.0, one sheet per functional block:\n  sheet 2  Bus and ports BUS INTERFACE: THE SIX PORTS' STROBES, THE CHIP'S CS, RS AND R/W, ITS DATA BUFFER\n  sheet 3  ACRTC and timing THE HD63484, THE DOT CLOCK, THE DOT COUNTER, P56 AND VALID\n  sheet 4  Frame memory ADDRESS LATCHES, THE TWO RAMS, THE FONT EPROM AND ITS COPY, THE MAD BUFFERS, THEIR CONTROL\n  sheet 5  Dots         THE GRAPHICS SHIFT REGISTERS AND THEIR LOAD, THE DELAY LINE, THE TWO LAYERS MIXED, THE DOT RETIMED\n  sheet 6  Control and video THE CONTROL REGISTER FROM THE ATTRIBUTE BYTE, THE THREE GUNS, THE SYNCS, THE VGA SOCKET\n  sheet 7  Text A       TEXT METHOD A: EIGHT SOCKETS, EMPTY ON THE FIRST BUILD\n  sheet 8  PS2          PS/2: ATMEGA328P, LATCHES ON PE / PF, THE CARD STATUS, FTDI, -INT, RESET\n  sheet 9  Power        POWER UNITS, DECOUPLING, POWER LED, THE F PARTS' PULL-UP\n\nEvery net of a sheet is a pin of its sheet symbol here, and the local label at each pin names the net\n(/NAME, the names on the board). Above the dashed line: the nets the sheet shares with other sheets (left:\nit reads them, right: it drives them). Below it: the nets drawn on that sheet only, a pin on each side\n(KiCad's ERC counts a root label as connected only when another label of its name is on the root sheet).\nVCC and GND are power symbols on the sheets." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 15.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9e616f4a-f2dd-5c02-a31c-ea0149245a64"))
	(sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
